ist when it comes to this  issue and this this relates to a lot of  different things it relates to not only  military action but it also relates to  issues of globalization and where  products are produced and how to what  degree we protect and prop up our  industry vs. operate in a world that we  recognized recognize is globalized and  often needs collectivist transnational  solutions that is my view and I think  that increasingly non-interventionism  isn't that much of a thing I mean it's  the debate mostly focuses on are we  isolationist sort of like the extreme  libertarians that you often see are we  interventionist like the neo cons and to  what degree do we push one policy or the  other but I think actually that the best  path forward is one of  non-interventionism we've got a great  bonus show for you today become a member  get instant access to the bonus show at  david pakman.com slash membership you do  get a free david pakman show  bumper-sticker  black or white if you sign up for a new  yearly membership and use the coupon  code vote soon 18 that'll save you 40%  and we will get you a free bumper  sticker just email us after you create  your membership say I want the black one  I want the white one here's my address  and we will get those bumper stickers  out to you
 

